===Etymology===
The origin and meaning of the name “Amuzgo” is unclear, and there are several theories. It seems likely that the name comes from one of the many Nahuatl languages ([[w:Uto-Aztecan languages|Uto-Aztecan]] language family): (1) One claim says that it comes from {{etyl|nah|en}} {{term|amoxco|lang=nah||Place of Books}}; (2) another is that it began as {{term|amuchco||where there is tin|lang=nah}}, composed of {{term|amuchitl||[[tin]]|lang=nah}} and {{term|-co||in, at|lang=nah}}; (3) a third idea is that it comes from {{etyl|nah|en}} {{term|amochitl||where there is [[copper]]|lang=nah}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# An indigenous language of Mexico ([[w:Oto-Manguean languages|Oto-Manguean language family]]) with about 30,000 speakers, mostly in Oaxaca state.

